import java.util.Random;

public class NFAPIDataProcessor {
  private static final int MAX_ELEMENTS = 10000;
  private static final Random RANDOM = new Random();

  public static NFAPI_CRC_INDICATION_PDU_T[] generateCrcIndicationPdus(int numElements) {
    if (numElements > MAX_ELEMENTS) {
      throw new IllegalArgumentException("Number of elements exceeds maximum allowed");
    }

    NFAPI_CRC_INDICATION_PDU_T[] pdus = new NFAPI_CRC_INDICATION_PDU_T[numElements];

    for (int i = 0; i < numElements; i++) {
      pdus[i] = new NFAPI_CRC_INDICATION_PDU_T();
      pdus[i].rxUeInformationTag = RANDOM.nextInt(100);
      pdus[i].rnti = RANDOM.nextInt(10000);
      pdus[i].crcIndicationRel8Tag = RANDOM.nextInt(100);
      pdus[i].crcFlag = RANDOM.nextBoolean();
    }

    return pdus;
  }
}
```
This method takes an integer `numElements` as input, which represents the number of elements to be generated in the array. It then creates a new array of `NFAPI_CRC_INDICATION_PDU_T` structures with the specified size and initializes each element with a random value for the `rxUeInformationTag`, `rnti`, and `crcIndicationRel8Tag`. The `crcFlag` is set to either 0 or 1 randomly.

