To fix this issue, we can use a lock-free data structure such as a circular buffer to store the `NFAPI_RX_FRAME_T` structures. This will allow multiple threads to access the array simultaneously without introducing any performance bottlenecks. Here's an example of how we can modify the code to use a lock-free circular buffer:
