To handle sudden spikes in traffic, such as those caused by network outages or emergency broadcasts, this implementation uses a self-healing mechanism that automatically recovers from failures by reallocating resources and restarting failed contexts. This mechanism detects failures without interrupting ongoing transactions and should be tested in various failure scenarios to ensure reliability.

