The function `allocateMemory()` is used to allocate memory for the transport channels and phy stats arrays. It takes two arguments: the number of transport channels and the number of phy stats. If either of these values is negative, the function will return an error message. Otherwise, it will allocate memory for the arrays using `malloc()`.

The function `deallocateMemory()` is used to deallocate memory for the transport channels and phy stats arrays. It simply calls `free()` on each array.

The function `addTransportChannel()` is used to add a new transport channel and its corresponding phy stats to the arrays. It takes four arguments: the TRANSPORT_CHANNEL_ID, BANDWIDTH, SCHEDULING_INSTANCE_TAG, and RB_UTILIZATION. If any of these values is negative, the function will return an error message. Otherwise, it will add a new transport channel to the array and update the corresponding phy stats.

The function `updateRbUtilization()` is used to update the rb utilization for a given transport channel and scheduling instance tag. It takes three arguments: the TRANSPORT_CHANNEL_ID, SCHEDULING_INSTANCE_TAG, and RB_UTILIZATION. If any of these values is negative, the function will return an error message. Otherwise, it will find the index of the transport channel in the array using a linear search, and then update the corresponding phy stats with the new rb utilization value.']

