3. Appends a slash (`/`) to the end of the string if it does not exceed the size limit, considering multi-byte character lengths. If the string length exceeds the size limit, the function closes the logging file descriptor and sets a flag in the configuration structure indicating an error occurred.
4. If the external configuration structure indicates strict mode is enabled, appends an additional space before the slash if the string length is less than half of the size limit, taking into account multi-byte characters. If the string length exceeds the size limit or the configuration structure does not indicate strict mode is enabled, the function closes the logging file descriptor and sets a flag in the configuration structure indicating an error occurred.
5. Returns the modified string if it fits within the size limit; otherwise, returns `NULL`.
6. Implements a mechanism to log errors or warnings to the specified file using the provided file descriptor, appending a timestamp and error message. The function ensures this does not affect the performance under high-frequency requests by using a separate thread for logging.
