The code also includes a mutex for protecting concurrent access to the buffer, which ensures that multiple threads can safely add and read telemetry data elements from the buffer without interfering with each other. The `init_circular_buffer()` function initializes the buffer with a given size, while the `destroy_circular_buffer()` function frees the memory allocated to the buffer when it is no longer needed.

The code also includes error handling for edge cases such as buffer overflow and invalid inputs, which are handled gracefully by returning an appropriate status code and providing detailed log messages upon failure.']

