This implementation uses a dynamic array for storing the UDP packets, which allows for efficient memory management and low-latency operations. The synchronization mechanism is implemented using pthreads mutexes and condition variables, which ensures thread safety without compromising performance. The function also includes a mechanism to merge the identifier, key, and packet arrays into a single sorted array based on the key values, and a mechanism to purge less frequently accessed records if the merged array size exceeds 750,000 elements. Additionally, the function prioritizes and processes high-priority packets immediately, ensuring data integrity and consistency during concurrent writes to the trace file. The solution is scalable to support varying levels of concurrent connections and can be easily extended to accommodate new features such as packet encryption or compression.']

