Comprehensive error handling strategies are implemented to manage unexpected input formats or missing fields gracefully, ensuring the function remains robust under varying conditions. Algorithmic choices are evaluated for their impact on system performance and resource consumption, aiming for a balance between speed and stability.

The function is designed with scalability and maintainability in mind, allowing for future enhancements and modifications without compromising functionality. Memory management practices are efficient, minimizing leaks and ensuring thread safety in multi-threaded environments.']

