This code defines a `manageLinkedList` function that dynamically manages a linked list of `NFAPI_CRC_INDICATION_PDU_T` structures. The function supports iterative operations such as inserting new elements at various positions in the list, deleting elements based on `RNTI`, and updating existing structures. It also implements a mechanism to gracefully handle memory resizing when the list exceeds a predefined size limit by reallocating memory and copying over the existing elements. The function is thread-safe to prevent concurrent access issues.

The `insertAtBeginning` function inserts a new element at the beginning of the list. It creates a new node with the given data and inserts it at the beginning of the list.

The `deleteByRNTI` function deletes an element from the list based on its RNTI. It iterates through the list until a node with the given RNTI is found, then deletes it from the list by updating its previous node's next pointer to point to the next node in the list.

The `updateByRNTI` function updates an element in the list based on its RNTI. It iterates through the list until a node with the given RNTI is found, then updates its data with the new values.

The `resizeList` function resizes the list when it exceeds a predefined size limit by reallocating memory and copying over the existing elements. It calculates the number of elements to be copied over, reallocates memory for the new list, copies over the existing elements, frees the old list, and sets the new list as the current list.

The `manageLinkedList`, `insertAtBeginning`, `deleteByRNTI`, `updateByRNTI`, and `resizeList` functions are all thread-safe to prevent concurrent access issues.']

