The class processes a large-scale user interaction log file containing structured event data, extracting relevant information and generating a summarized report. Developers can optimize the class to handle varying levels of user activity and adapt resource allocation accordingly. The class accepts several parameters: the name of the input log file, the name of the output report file, a string specifying the filter criteria for active sessions, a boolean flag indicating whether to include detailed session logs in the report, a numeric threshold for purging inactive sessions, and a flag indicating whether the log file should be processed asynchronously.

The class manages dynamic arrays for storing 'String' session IDs, 'String' user IP addresses, 'long' timestamps, 'int' session durations, and 'boolean' status flags. Each session structure contains multiple fields, and the class should handle the allocation and resizing of these arrays efficiently to accommodate up to 10 million elements per array, ensuring optimal performance even under high load conditions. The class also implements a mechanism to merge the 'sessionID', 'userID', 'loginTime', 'logoutTime', and 'duration' arrays into a single sorted array based on the 'logoutTime' values. If the merged array size exceeds 750,000 elements, trigger a system log warning and initiate a process to purge inactive sessions to maintain performance and resource utilization.

